	'register' => 'The whole site is formal dumneavoastră, in every string and every slot — body copy, headings, eyebrows, ALL-CAPS bands, buttons, form labels, placeholders, alt and aria text, the <title>, the meta description, og: tags and JSON-LD. Register is a property of the PAGE, not of the segment: a tu-form in a meta description contradicts the dumneavoastră body it ships with. The verb is second-person plural and a predicative adjective agreeing with the reader is plural: „Ne puteți suna”, „Sunteți pregătiți…?” — never „Nu sunteți sigur”. The reader-facing possessive is „dumneavoastră”, always in full, never „dvs.”. No tu form (tău, ta, tine, poți, vrei, vezi, începi) appears anywhere, at any length. Do not chop Romanian subordinate-clause sentences into fragments; an impersonal construction („se poate configura”) often reads better than an imperative in descriptive prose. BUTTONS AND LINK LABELS keep the verb of the English and use the polite plural imperative, standard Romanian web UI: „Browse catalog” = „Consultați catalogul”, „Request a demo” = „Solicitați o demonstrație”, „Download” = „Descărcați”, „Contact us” = „Contactați-ne”, „Search” = „Căutați”. Never flatten a verb label into a bare noun („Catalog”, „Descărcare” are wrong for those), and a control label carries no pronoun or possessive („Protejați-vă investiția” is wrong; „Protecția investiției” is right). Everything that is not a control label addresses the reader only as dumneavoastră.',
